@@ -20,3 +20,19 @@ Vanilla JavaScript (no preprocessors). Cucumber + happy-dom for verification. np
 - localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs`.
 - Routing: hash-based (`#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`). No routing library needed; vanilla `hashchange` listener suffices.
 - Tier: happy-dom (cheapest sufficient to observe DOM-level behaviour).
+
+## Acceptance Defects (browser-only, fixed acceptance suite)
+
+Three product defects reported by the external browser acceptance suite that happy-dom does not reproduce:
+
+1. **Variable-function name collision (`toggleAll`)**: `var toggleAll` (the `#toggle-all` DOM element) shadows `function toggleAll()`. The click handler calls the element as a function. Fix: rename one of the two — the variable to `toggleAllCheckbox` or the function to `toggleAllTodos`.
+
+2. **Full-list re-render destroys DOM nodes**: `render()` does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` then recreates all `<li>` elements. Any browser-held reference to a node becomes detached after any state change. Fix: mutate existing nodes in place (toggle classes, update checkbox `checked`) instead of destroying and recreating the list on every change.
+
+3. **Toggle-all not hidden during editing**: The app-spec says "When editing mode is activated it will hide the other controls." The `#toggle-all` checkbox is not hidden when a todo enters editing mode. Fix: set `toggleAll.style.display = 'none'` (or `.main .toggle-all` parent) when any `<li>` has the `editing` class, and restore it otherwise.
+
+## Planted Specs
+
+`specs/todos-dom-stability.feature` pins DOM node identity preservation across toggle, toggle-all, clear-completed, and add operations; and pins the toggle-all visibility during editing. These scenarios require new step definitions in `specs/support/` to verify DOM node identity (e.g. capturing a node reference, performing an action, then asserting the same reference is still in the DOM).
+
+`watchbill.json` watch5 covers these scenarios.
