@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Browser DOM stability
+  As a user interacting with the app in a real browser
+  I want the DOM to remain stable across state changes
+  So that my interaction flow is not interrupted by element replacement
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: DOM node identity is preserved during toggle
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves DOM node identity
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list item at position 1 is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+
+    Scenario: Toggling all todos preserves DOM node identity
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles all todos on
+      Then every todo list item is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+
+    Scenario: Clearing completed preserves DOM node identity of remaining items
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user clicks clear-completed
+      Then the todo list item at position 1 is the same DOM node as before the clear
+
+    Scenario: Adding a todo preserves DOM node identity of existing items
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user adds a todo "Walk dog"
+      Then the todo list item at position 1 is the same DOM node as before the add
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all hidden during editing
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox is hidden when editing a todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not visible
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox is visible when not editing
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is visible
